NOTE on bibliographic references
We encourage contributors to provide bibliographic references to a construction entry. For this, we create bibliographic entries, collect them in a bibliography, and attach this bibliography to the metadata of the construction.

The description of a bibliographic entry roughly follows the format adopted by the Bibliography of Linguistic Literature. Following their entries, a bibliographic entry uses dc:creator (for authors), dc:title (for title), dc:type (for the type of entry, e.g., JOUR for journal), dcterms:issued (for publication year), dcterms:publisher (for publisher), dcterms:isPartOf (for journal), bibo:volume (for volume number), bibo:issue (for issue number), bibo:pages (for page range) and dc:identifier (for DOIs).
The Bibliography of Linguistic Literature (BLL): https://data.linguistik.de/en/
BLLDB (the online version of the BLL): https://www.blldb-online.de/blldb/templates/template.xml?vid=9EC46B92-A6E0-421A-B817-154FAC462A88&contenttype=text/html&Skript=home
Whenever possible, we retrieve this information directly from Crossref.
The URI of the bibliographic entry uses the prefix references: (https://bdlweb.phil.uni-erlangen.de/RCxn/Abox/references#).
